{"question_id":"l7KivpauqXUjtsH3gl1kltjud4z","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th February Morning Shift","year":2021,"subject":"physics","chapter":"current-electricity","chapterGroup":"electricity","type":"integer","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"content":"In an electrical circuit, a battery is connected to pass 20C of charge through it in a certain given time. The potential difference between two plates of the battery is maintained at 15V. The workdone by the battery is __________J.","options":[],"correct_options":[],"explanation":"<p>Given, charge passing through circuit, q = 20 C</p>\n<p>Potential difference between two plates,</p>\n<p>V = 15 V</p>\n<p>Let W be the amount of work done by battery.</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> W = qV = 20 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.02ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.09ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -491 778 482\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 15 = 300 J</p>","qKey":"l7KivpauqXUjtsH3gl1kltjud4z","paperKey":"jee-main-2021-online-26th-february-morning-slot","exam":"jee-main","questions":[{"question_id":"l7KivpauqXUjtsH3gl1kltjud4z","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th F